tage2_template/TASK.md</a></p></td></tr><tr><th>Output</th><td><strong>Complete repaired RTL module.</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><details><summary>Read input: stage2_template/design.v · <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00539&amp;file=stage2_template%2Fdesign.v'>Open raw</a></summary><pre>module mg_04586 (x, y);\ninput [31:0] x; \n  output [31:0] y; \n  assign y[31:29] = ~(x[6:4] ^ x[17:15]); \n  assign y[28:0] = {x[3:0], x[31:7]} ^ {x[14:0],x[31:18]} ^ x[31:3]; \n endmodule</pre></details></div></div><div class=\"flow\"><strong>Stage 1 output → abstraction gate → fresh Stage 2 input.</strong> The intermediate text is generated separately for each model/attempt. It is not a prefilled golden description. Stage 2 receives neither the clean RTL nor the Stage 1 conversation.</div><h2>Private final evaluation</h2><div class=\"card\"><table><tbody><tr><th style=\"width:175px\">Reference RTL</th><td><a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00539&amp;file=private%2Fgolden.v'>private/golden.v</a></td></tr><tr><th style=\"width:175px\">Score / oracle</th><td>Binary formal equivalence to the hidden clean module</td></tr></tbody></table><p class=\"muted\">The formal oracle consumes the complete Stage 2 RTL file and compares it with the clean reference. A golden RTL file is scoring material, not a generated Stage 1 output.</p></div>"}, "files": [{"name": "case.json", "url": "assets/f53a55ae6a3cb7e3339b0de8151a53e3af3417f7feff1f075e4d054eea88592d.txt", "size": 4488, "binary": false, "section": "Other: case.json"}, {"name": "private/equivalence.ys", "url": "assets/af6ee848b75588e50afc5b1b25a20a3b5b3b857b8159b69dcdb610dea57bbd5c.txt", "size": 595, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/golden.v", "url": "assets/1ec46641e3cf480034eff4c02372ef618081d8b0371159158cabbf3c44252c00.txt", "size": 181, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/qualification/negative/equivalence.ys", "url": "assets/af6ee848b75588e50afc5b